      "description": "Watch Botafogo vs Athletico Paranaense highlights and goals from Brasileirão on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The encounter between Botafogo and Athletico Paranaense promised a fierce contest as both teams aimed to climb the table in this mid-season Serie A battle. On August 25, 2026 , fans gathered to witness a match defined by clinical finishing and a dramatic late surge that kept everyone guessing until the final whistle. A Clinical First Half Display Athletico Paranaense wasted no time establishing dominance in the opening stages. The visitors took the lead in the 11th minute when Joao Cruz found the back of the net with a precise finish. Before the home side could even regroup, they were hit with a second blow just two minutes later. In the 13th minute, Dantas turned provider, setting up Kevin Viveros to double the lead and leave the Botafogo faithful in shock. The first half continued to be a struggle for the hosts. Tactically outmaneuvered, their frustration boiled over in the 35th minute when Kauan Toledo received a yellow card for a cynical challenge. While Botafogo attempted to construct attacks, the visitors' defense remained resolute, heading into the break with a commanding two-goal cushion. Tactical Shifts and Viveros Strikes Again Both managers looked to their benches at the start of the second half, with Botafogo introducing Junior Santos and Juan Portilla to inject some energy. Despite the changes, the momentum remained largely with the visitors. Edenilson picked up a yellow card for the hosts in the 68th minute as they struggled to contain the counter-attacking threat of the \"Furacão.\" In the 78th minute, it appeared the game was beyond reach. Kerwin Vargas delivered a brilliant assist for Kevin Viveros , who made no mistake in securing his second goal of the night. With the scoreboard reading 3-0 in favor of Athletico Paranaense , many expected a quiet finish to the proceedings. Stoppage Time Drama However, the match was far from over. Santiago Rodriguez , who had come on as a substitute, sparked a late revival for Botafogo . In the 85th minute, he pulled one back to give the home fans a glimmer of hope. The atmosphere shifted instantly as the hosts threw men forward in a desperate attempt to salvage a point. In the second minute of stoppage time, the tension reached a breaking point. Danilo found Santiago Rodriguez once again, and the forward clinicaly converted to make it 3-2. The final minutes were played at a frantic pace, but the referee's final whistle at 90+6' brought the comeback attempt to a halt. Athletico Paranaense escaped with all three points after a resilient defensive stand in the dying moments."
